        "Kd_att": [
          20.0,
          50.0,
          50.0
        ],
        "max_tilt_deg": 45.0,
        "heading": "from_plant_hover_convention",
        "role": "Low-speed practical baseline, design region 0-20 m/s (configs/arena.json controllers.CPID.design_region_m_s). Excluded from main-test scenarios that go above the region (kj decision 2026-09-26); the high-speed limit of linear fixed-gain control is GSLQR's role.",
        "design_note": "Tilt limit is measured from world vertical. The trim thrust axis is 33.4 deg (controller model) / 34.1 deg (plant) from vertical at 20 m/s and 45.1 deg at 25 m/s, so with the PX4 default 45 deg the design region 0-20 m/s keeps ~11 deg of margin. No aero feed-forward: the integrators carry the aerodynamic share of the trim (20 m/s: 4.63 m/s^2 horizontal, 2.85 m/s^2 vertical), so the arena preloads them from the controller-model trim (configs/arena.json controllers.CPID.integrator_preload).",
        "integrator_note": "Both integrators (horizontal velocity, altitude) are limited as ACCELERATION AUTHORITY in m/s^2 (1 g), independent of Ki, and are frozen while the command is tilt- or rotor-limited (paper sec 5.3 conditional integration). PX4 PositionControl limits only the VERTICAL velocity integral to +-1 g (CONSTANTS_ONE_G) and uses tracking anti-windup with no fixed magnitude in the horizontal plane; the horizontal +-1 g here extends PX4's vertical criterion to the horizontal plane. It never binds inside the design region (design check: limit -> infinity is bit-identical). a_int_z_max=null restores the legacy altitude integrator (unconditional, state limit int_z_max in m*s = 2.5 m/s^2 at Ki_z 0.5).",
        "feedforward_note": "Reference-acceleration feed-forward (configs/arena.json controllers.CPID.reference_feedforward = window_acceleration): a_des = a_ref + velocity PID, the same structure as PX4 PositionControl (setInputSetpoint puts the trajectory acceleration in _acc_sp and _velocityControl adds the PID output to it; checked in PX4 main 7c8d6daca9be). a_ref is the forward difference of the reference velocity over the NMPC's first prediction interval (0.05 s) of the same reference window the NMPCs read. Class default off (legacy bit-identical); with a constant reference a_ref is exactly 0 and the path is skipped.",
        "change_record": "2026-09-26 kj decision: velocity integral limit 5 -> 9.81 m/s^2, altitude integral legacy -> 9.81 m/s^2 conditional, plus integrator preload. 2026-09-26 kj decision: max_tilt_deg 35 -> 45 = PX4 default MPC_TILTMAX_AIR (checked in PX4 main, src/modules/mc_pos_control/multicopter_position_control_limits_params.yaml: default 45.0) because the manuscript describes CPID as the PX4 structure and the 20 m/s trim (33.4 deg) sat at the edge of 35 deg; class default stays 35 (legacy bit-identical). 2026-09-26 afternoon kj decision 2: reference-acceleration feed-forward (see feedforward_note) after the new tuning ramp 0->15 showed CPID window RMSE v 2.72 vs 0.035-0.58 for the others. All of these were made AFTER seeing results, OUTSIDE the tuning budget, in CPID's FAVOUR (baseline-strengthening). Recorded in the fairness table of results/ARENA_STATUS; before/after in results/arena/FEEDFORWARD.md."
      }
